  "worked_solution": "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12+1 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
